Quantized-LingBot-Map

This project is derived from LingBot-Map by Robbyant and its contributors:
https://github.com/Robbyant/lingbot-map
LingBot-Map is distributed under the Apache License 2.0. Original source
copyright and attribution notices are retained in the copied files.

The quantization implementation follows QuantVGGT's local Hadamard rotation,
channel smoothing, learned weight clipping and learned activation clipping:
https://github.com/wlfeng0509/QuantVGGT
QuantVGGT is distributed under the Apache License 2.0. Streaming state capture,
calibrated direct W4A4, packed inference, compressed KV storage and the project
command-line tools are adaptations in this repository.

Native signed INT4 GEMM uses NVIDIA CUTLASS v3.5.1, installed separately:
https://github.com/NVIDIA/cutlass
CUTLASS retains its own BSD-3-Clause license. It is not bundled here.

The CUDA/streaming model integration and image loading files contain local
modifications. Evaluation adapters retain the LingBot-Map metric definitions.
The included result figures are derived from the TUM RGB-D dataset and the
Indoor Travel evaluation sequence. TUM RGB-D dataset attribution:
J. Sturm et al., A Benchmark for the Evaluation of RGB-D SLAM Systems, IROS 2012.
https://cvg.cit.tum.de/data/datasets/rgbd-dataset

Model checkpoints and datasets are obtained separately under their original
terms. This repository does not redistribute weights, videos or image datasets.
